<task id="003" project="smart-todo-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>Convert LegalWorkspace SmartToDo/ to a thin shim consuming @spaarke/smart-todo-components (FR-01)</title>
    <phase>1: Shared-lib foundation</phase>
    <gate>002 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Final step of the Phase-1 critical-path hoist spine; downstream Phase 2/3/4 tasks (012, 020, 022, 023, 024, 034) all depend on this task landing cleanly. Removes/rewrites LW-local source and updates real consumers (`workspaceConfig.tsx`, `App.tsx`).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical conversion task (re-export + import-path swap) following the exact shim pattern already proven by `todo.registration.ts`/`SmartTodoWidget` — well-specified, not architecturally novel like tasks 001/002.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial spine (001→002→003) — this task consumes the exact package shape task 002 produces; cannot run concurrently with it or with anything else touching `Spaarke.SmartTodo.Components` or LW's `SmartToDo/`.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002</deps>
